.MARINE...
(Today through Friday)
Issued at 837 AM PST Sun Nov 22 2026

A cold front moved through the coastal waters this morning. Behind
the front winds have shifted to a moderate northerly breeze with
moderate to rough seas and scattered showers. Starting Monday
winds will shift back to southerly and increase in strength as a
stronger cold front approaches the coast. Wind speed will peak
just ahead of the front on Tuesday, with gale force gusts
possible. These winds will be followed by building rough to very
rough seas, eventually exceeding 15 feet across all exposed
waters on Wednesday.

